---
import Heading from "@/components/Typography/Heading.astro";
interface Props {
  /** Set to `false` to skip rendering this component and its children. */
  render?: boolean;
}
const { render = true } = Astro.props;
---

{
  render && (
    <div class="searchdemo_wrap">
      <div class="searchdemo_top">
        <>
          <span>KeepIndex / your workspace</span>
          <span>Illustrative example · sample data</span>
        </>
      </div>
      <div class="searchdemo_query">
        <>
          <span aria-hidden="true">⌕</span>
          <p>What did I learn about restoring my backups?</p>
          <span class="searchdemo_scope">This computer</span>
        </>
      </div>
      <div
        class="searchdemo_tabs"
        role="tablist"
        aria-label="Example result mode"
      >
        <button
          type="button"
          role="tab"
          id="example-search-tab"
          aria-controls="example-search"
          aria-selected="true"
        >
          Search
        </button>
        <button
          type="button"
          role="tab"
          id="example-answer-tab"
          aria-controls="example-answer"
          aria-selected="false"
          tabindex="-1"
        >
          Answer
        </button>
        <button
          type="button"
          role="tab"
          id="example-research-tab"
          aria-controls="example-research"
          aria-selected="false"
          tabindex="-1"
        >
          Research
        </button>
      </div>
      <div class="searchdemo_body">
        <div
          role="tabpanel"
          id="example-search"
          aria-labelledby="example-search-tab"
          tabindex="0"
        >
          <div class="searchdemo_result">
            <>
              <span class="searchdemo_kind">VAULT · Markdown</span>
              <Heading tag="h3" variant="h4">
                A backup is only useful if I can restore it
              </Heading>
              <p>
                Run a restore drill before relying on a backup. Keep the
                recovery instructions next to the checklist.
              </p>
              <small>notes / backup-drill.md</small>
            </>
          </div>
          <div class="searchdemo_result">
            <>
              <span class="searchdemo_kind">FILES · Text</span>
              <Heading tag="h3" variant="h4">
                Weekend restore checklist
              </Heading>
              <p>
                Restore into an empty folder. Compare checksums. Record the
                recovery time.
              </p>
              <small>projects / restore-checklist.txt</small>
            </>
          </div>
          <div class="searchdemo_result">
            <>
              <span class="searchdemo_kind">HISTORY · Visited page</span>
              <Heading tag="h3" variant="h4">
                Restoring from a backup — restic documentation
              </Heading>
              <p>
                A page you visited about restoring snapshots and choosing a
                destination.
              </p>
              <small>restic.readthedocs.io · title and visit metadata</small>
            </>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div
          role="tabpanel"
          id="example-answer"
          aria-labelledby="example-answer-tab"
          tabindex="0"
          hidden
        >
          <>
            <span class="searchdemo_kind">ANSWER · Local model example</span>
            <Heading tag="h3" variant="h3">
              Practice the recovery, too.
            </Heading>
          </>
          <p>
            Your notes emphasize testing a restore before you rely on a backup.
            Keep the recovery steps beside the checklist.{" "}
            <a href="#example-source-one">[L1]</a>
          </p>
          <p>
            Your checklist adds three concrete steps: restore into an empty
            folder, compare checksums, and record how long it takes.{" "}
            <a href="#example-source-two">[L2]</a>
          </p>
          <details id="example-source-one">
            <>
              <summary>[L1] Inspect the note</summary>
              <blockquote>
                “Run a restore drill before relying on a backup. Keep the
                recovery instructions next to the checklist.”
              </blockquote>
              <small>Sample source: notes / backup-drill.md</small>
            </>
          </details>
          <details id="example-source-two">
            <>
              <summary>[L2] Inspect the checklist</summary>
              <blockquote>
                “Restore into an empty folder. Compare checksums. Record the
                recovery time.”
              </blockquote>
              <small>Sample source: projects / restore-checklist.txt</small>
            </>
          </details>
        </div>
        <div
          role="tabpanel"
          id="example-research"
          aria-labelledby="example-research-tab"
          tabindex="0"
          hidden
        >
          <>
            <span class="searchdemo_kind">
              RESEARCH · Example investigation
            </span>
            <Heading tag="h3" variant="h3">
              Turn scattered notes into a plan.
            </Heading>
          </>
          <ol>
            <>
              <li>
                <strong>Find the advice.</strong> Read your backup drill note
                and restore checklist.
              </li>
              <li>
                <strong>Compare the steps.</strong> Connect recovery
                instructions with the checksum and timing checks.
              </li>
              <li>
                <strong>Identify the gap.</strong> These example notes contain
                no measured recovery time. Run a drill before estimating one.
              </li>
            </>
          </ol>
          <p class="searchdemo_caveat">
            Real results depend on your sources and model. Citations help you
            inspect an answer; they do not guarantee it is correct.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="searchdemo_bottom">
        This example runs entirely in this page. It does not access your files,
        history, or local KeepIndex installation.
      </div>
    </div>
  )
}
<script>
  document.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>(".searchdemo_wrap").forEach((root) => {
    const tabs = Array.from(
      root.querySelectorAll<HTMLButtonElement>('[role="tab"]'),
    );
    const select = (tab: HTMLButtonElement) => {
      tabs.forEach((item) => {
        const active = item === tab;
        item.setAttribute("aria-selected", String(active));
        item.tabIndex = active ? 0 : -1;
      });
      root
        .querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('[role="tabpanel"]')
        .forEach((panel) => {
          panel.hidden = panel.id !== tab.getAttribute("aria-controls");
        });
    };
    tabs.forEach((tab, index) => {
      tab.addEventListener("click", () => select(tab));
      tab.addEventListener("keydown", (event) => {
        if (!["ArrowRight", "ArrowLeft", "Home", "End"].includes(event.key))
          return;
        event.preventDefault();
        const next =
          event.key === "Home"
            ? 0
            : event.key === "End"
              ? tabs.length - 1
              : (index + (event.key === "ArrowRight" ? 1 : -1) + tabs.length) %
                tabs.length;
        const target = tabs[next];
        if (target) {
          select(target);
          target.focus();
        }
      });
    });
    root
      .querySelectorAll<HTMLAnchorElement>('a[href^="#example-source-"]')
      .forEach((link) =>
        link.addEventListener("click", () => {
          const detail = root.querySelector<HTMLDetailsElement>(
            link.getAttribute("href")!,
          );
          if (detail) detail.open = true;
        }),
      );
  });
</script>
<style is:global>
  @layer components {
    .searchdemo_wrap {
      width: 100%;
      background: #fcfaf3;
      color: #13211a;
      border: 0.0625rem solid #c7c9b9;
      border-radius: 0.75rem;
      overflow: hidden;
      .searchdemo_top,
      .searchdemo_bottom {
        padding: 1rem 1.5rem;
        font-size: 0.7rem;
        color: #52604e;
        background: #eeefe4;
      }
      .searchdemo_top {
        display: flex;
        justify-content: space-between;
        gap: 1rem;
      }
      .searchdemo_query {
        margin: 1.5rem;
        border: 0.0625rem solid #b8c1ac;
        border-radius: 0.4rem;
        padding: 1rem;
        display: flex;
        align-items: center;
        gap: 0.75rem;
      }
      .searchdemo_query > span:first-child {
        font-size: 1.75rem;
      }
      .searchdemo_query p {
        font-size: 1.1rem;
        font-weight: 550;
      }
      .searchdemo_scope {
        margin-left: auto;
        white-space: nowrap;
        font-size: 0.65rem;
        padding: 0.4rem 0.6rem;
        border-radius: 0.25rem;
        background: #dcebd8;
      }
      .searchdemo_tabs {
        display: flex;
        gap: 1.5rem;
        padding: 0 1.5rem;
        border-bottom: 0.0625rem solid #d4d7c8;
      }
      .searchdemo_tabs button {
        padding: 0.75rem 0.25rem;
        color: #52604e;
        border-bottom: 0.15rem solid transparent;
        font-size: 0.85rem;
        cursor: pointer;
      }
      .searchdemo_tabs button[aria-selected="true"] {
        color: #13211a;
        border-color: #28793b;
        font-weight: 600;
      }
      .searchdemo_body {
        padding: 1.5rem;
        min-height: 27rem;
      }
      .searchdemo_result + .searchdemo_result {
        border-top: 0.0625rem solid #d4d7c8;
        margin-top: 1.25rem;
        padding-top: 1.25rem;
      }
      .searchdemo_kind {
        font-family: monospace;
        font-size: 0.65rem;
        color: #28793b;
        letter-spacing: 0.07em;
        display: block;
        margin-bottom: 0.6rem;
      }
      p {
        font-size: 0.95rem;
        line-height: 1.7;
        max-width: 75ch;
        margin: 0.5rem 0;
      }
      small {
        color: #52604e;
        font-size: 0.7rem;
      }
      a {
        color: #28793b;
        text-decoration: underline;
      }
      details {
        margin-top: 1rem;
        border: 0.0625rem solid #d4d7c8;
        border-radius: 0.3rem;
        padding: 0.75rem 1rem;
        font-size: 0.85rem;
      }
      summary {
        cursor: pointer;
        font-weight: 550;
      }
      blockquote {
        border-left: 0.15rem solid #28793b;
        padding-left: 1rem;
        margin: 1rem 0;
        line-height: 1.7;
      }
      ol {
        padding-left: 1.25rem;
        margin-top: 1rem;
      }
      li {
        padding: 0.65rem 0;
        line-height: 1.7;
      }
      .searchdemo_caveat {
        padding-top: 1.5rem;
        color: #52604e;
      }
      @media (width < 48rem) {
        .searchdemo_top {
          flex-direction: column;
          gap: 0.3rem;
        }
        .searchdemo_scope {
          display: none;
        }
        .searchdemo_body {
          min-height: 32rem;
          padding: 1rem;
        }
        .searchdemo_query {
          margin: 1rem;
        }
      }
    }
  }
</style>
